{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceTraces"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_FE_differ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_FE_differ","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L126-L129","doc":"**Ordering matters, classically.** Taken alone, `FE` has different traces on the two spaces:\nalready for the empty word they differ by `3`, independent of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_symmetric_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_symmetric_eq","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L118-L124","doc":"**Symmetric insertion.** `FE + EF` has equal plain traces on the two weight spaces for every\nbraid word, so it adds nothing to the `K`-weight ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_EFn_eq_FEp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_EFn_eq_FEp","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L113-L116","doc":"… and `EF` on the neutron space matches `FE` on the proton space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_FEn_eq_EFp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.trace_FEn_eq_EFp","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L107-L111","doc":"**State-swapped traces.** For every braid word, `FE` on the neutron space has the same\nplain trace as `EF` on the proton space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.intertwine_FE_EF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.intertwine_FE_EF","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L85-L88","doc":"`P` sends `FE` on the proton space to `EF` on the neutron space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.intertwine_EF_FE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.intertwine_EF_FE","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L80-L83","doc":"`P` sends `EF` on the proton space to `FE` on the neutron space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn_sector","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L73-L78","doc":"Sector scalars on the neutron space: `EF` has the same roots `0` and `[3]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEp_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEp_sector","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L66-L71","doc":"Sector scalars on the proton space: `FE` has roots `0` and `[3] = q² + 1 + q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn_comm₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn_comm₂","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L62-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn_comm₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn_comm₁","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L58-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEp_comm₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEp_comm₂","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L54-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEp_comm₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEp_comm₁","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L50-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEn_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEn_eq","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L46-L48","doc":"… and by `-1` on the `(1,2)` space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFp_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFp_eq","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The commutator `[E, F] = (K - K⁻¹)/(q - q⁻¹)` acts by `+1` on the `(2,1)` space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.EFn","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L39-L40","doc":"`EF` on the `(1,2)` weight space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.FEn","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/NucleonWeightSpaceSecondOrder.lean#L37-L38","doc":"`FE` on the `(1,2)` weight space. 